CPU backend: what the model and CLI need to run on liblernex_cpu.so (git apply -p1 from the repo root;
text before the first "diff --git" is ignored).

Measured with exactly this diff applied, on the lernex server's i5-14500 (14 threads, AVX-VNNI level):
Praxis BF16 and INT8 run end to end on the CPU inside the BF16 noise floor (numbers in the CPU
workstream's report). Nothing here changes what the CUDA build computes.

What the model needs from the runtime ABI, and what this diff does about it:

1. No CUDA runtime calls in the model. metis.cpp/metis.h use cudaMalloc/cudaMemset/cudaMemcpy,
   cudaMallocHost, events, cudaMemsetAsync and graph capture directly. They become lx_rt_alloc
   (zeroed), lx_rt_copy, lx_rt_memset, lx_rt_host_alloc, lx_rt_event_*, and lx_rt_capture_* with
   cudaStream_t -> void* in metis.h. Capture: when lx_rt_capture_begin answers LX_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED
   the model stops trying and runs every step eagerly (the CPU backend's answer). The CPU runtime does
   not record that answer as lx_rt_last_error, since eval checks lx_rt_last_error after a run.

2. The four glue kernels (glue.cu: axpby, sub, meta_scalars, gather_last) are CUDA. This diff adds
   glue_cpu.cpp (the same four as loops) and builds it instead of glue.cu in the CPU-only build.
   Recommendation: move them into kernels.h as ABI ops (lx_axpby_f32, lx_sub_f32, lx_meta_scalars,
   lx_gather_last) so every backend library exports them and one lernex binary can dlopen any
   backend; the CPU versions are the loops in glue_cpu.cpp.

3. Zero-copy weights. Weights::upload asks lx_rt_backend(); on the CPU the tensors point into the
   safetensors mapping (the set must outlive the Weights, which eval and inspect already do) and
   nothing is copied. LX_COPY_WEIGHTS=1 copies anyway, into lx_rt_alloc memory (huge pages on Linux).

4. cli/eval.cpp and cli/inspect.cpp use lx_rt_* instead of the CUDA runtime (inspect prints the
   backend and lx_arch instead of the GPU name and free VRAM, which have no ABI call).

5. CMake: with -DLX_BACKEND_CUDA=OFF -DLX_BACKEND_CPU=ON, lernex_core and the lernex CLI build
   against liblernex_cpu.so; the CUDA build filters *_cpu.cpp out of its sources.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index b169552..79ffa4e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -26,6 +26,19 @@ if(LX_BACKEND_CPU)
   add_subdirectory(engine/cpu)
 endif()
 
+# The model and CLI on the CPU backend alone, where there is no CUDA: lernex linked to liblernex_cpu.so.
+# The glue kernels the model wires between library calls come from glue_cpu.cpp instead of glue.cu.
+if(LX_BACKEND_CPU AND NOT LX_BACKEND_CUDA)
+  file(GLOB LX_CPU_CORE_SOURCES CONFIGURE_DEPENDS engine/core/*.cpp engine/model/*.cpp engine/runtime/*.cpp
+       engine/text/*.cpp engine/server/*.cpp)
+  add_library(lernex_core STATIC ${LX_CPU_CORE_SOURCES})
+  target_include_directories(lernex_core PUBLIC engine third_party)
+  target_link_libraries(lernex_core PUBLIC lernex_cpu)
+  file(GLOB LX_CLI_SOURCES CONFIGURE_DEPENDS cli/*.cpp)
+  add_executable(lernex ${LX_CLI_SOURCES})
+  target_link_libraries(lernex PRIVATE lernex_core)
+endif()
+
 if(NOT LX_BACKEND_CUDA)
   return()
 endif()
@@ -46,6 +59,7 @@ target_link_libraries(lernex_kernels PUBLIC CUDA::cudart CUDA::cublasLt)
 # The runtime: config, weights, the Metis model, caches and the scheduler.
